##  Project Structure

```
vacancy_project/                # Main project directory
│
├── jobs/                       # Django app for vacancy management
│   ├── admin.py                # Django admin
│   ├── models.py               # Vacancy, UserVacancy
│   ├── services.py             # Saving vacancies (one transaction)
│   ├── filters.py              # Shared filter rules
│   ├── exceptions.py           # ParserError
│   ├── views.py                # Views
│   │
│   ├── management/
│   │   └── commands/
│   │       ├── run_all.py      # Run all parsers
│   │       └── run_bot.py      # Run the Telegram bot
│   │
│   ├── migrations/             # Database migrations (keep them in git)
│   │
│   └── parsers/                # One scraper per job site
│       ├── dou.py              # RSS feed
│       ├── jooble.py           # API
│       ├── work.py             # Selenium
│       ├── robota.py           # Playwright (disabled)
│       └── indeed.py           # Not connected yet
│
├── telegram_bot/               # Telegram bot logic
│   └── bot.py
│
├── templates/
│   └── admin/jobs/vacancy/change_list.html
│
├── vacancy_project/            # Django project configuration
│   ├── settings.py
│   ├── urls.py
│   ├── views.py                # Guest login
│   └── wsgi.py
│
├── .env                        # Secrets (not in git)
├── manage.py
├── Procfile                    # Render start command
└── README
```

---

##  Known limits

- **Robota.ua is disabled.** Cloudflare asks "confirm you are human" and blocks the automatic browser.
- **Indeed** has a parser file, but it is not connected to `run_all`.
- Keyword filters cannot read the full text of a vacancy. A language-model check is planned for this.

---

## Deployment (Render)

- Build Command: pip install -r requirements.txt && python manage.py migrate && python manage.py collectstatic --noinput
- Start command: see Procfile (gunicorn).
- Django migrations are applied during the build, so the database tables are updated on each deploy.
- Local and Render use the same Supabase PostgreSQL database, so be careful with deleting data.
- Work.ua needs Chrome, which is usually not installed on Render. There this parser will report a `ParserError`, and the other sources still work.

The app is available at:

- **Admin access**: [https://vacancy-project.onrender.com/](https://vacancy-project.onrender.com/)
  *(requires an administrator account)*
- **Guest access**: [https://vacancy-project.onrender.com/demo/](https://vacancy-project.onrender.com/demo/)
  *(automatic login as a guest user)*